## Request Flow

POST /agent/message
        ↓
orchestrator.py
  1. load_full_memory()       → last 20 interactions + patient profile
  2. get_recent_turns(n=3)    → for intent router only
  3. route_intent()           → classify message
  4. EMERGENCY? → escalate_to_caregiver() → return immediately
  5. agent.invoke()           → agent picks tools and responds
  6. save_interaction()       → log to Supabase
  7. return AgentResponse

---

## Use Cases

| Route     | Example                        | What Happens                          |
|-----------|--------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| DB        | "What are my medications?"     | Agent calls DB tools                  |
| RAG       | "What is Alzheimer's?"         | Agent calls search_knowledge_base     |
| DB_RAG    | "Is my medication safe?"       | Agent calls DB + RAG, merges answer   |
| LLM       | "I feel lonely"                | Agent responds, no tools              |
| CLARIFY   | Unclear message                | Agent gently asks patient to repeat   |
| EMERGENCY | "I fell" / "I'm in pain"       | Orchestrator bypasses agent, alerts caregiver |

---

## Memory Rules
- Short-term → LangChain ConversationBufferMemory, RAM only, per session
- Interaction log → Supabase, saved after every turn
- Patient profile → Supabase, updated at session end using last 3 turns only
- Agent gets last 20 interactions at session start
- Intent router gets last 3 turns only

---

## Tool Rules
- LangChain tools (agent picks): db_tools, rag_tool, confusion_tool
- Internal only (not agent-facing): sql_validator, escalate_to_caregiver
- SQL is always validated before execution
- No tool called more than once per turn for the same data
- Tool failures → graceful response, never expose errors to patient

---

## Hard Rules
- EMERGENCY is always handled by orchestrator — agent never sees it
- RAG is external — send query, receive chunks only
- Never fabricate patient data — always fetch from DB
- Never expose tool names, SQL, or system internals to the patient
- Never advise medication changes or give medical advice beyond the knowledge base

---

## Stack
FastAPI, langchain framwork for the agent, LangChain ReAct , Db Supabase(postgresql), GPT-4o for the intent classification,APScheduler for reminders , Pydantic